From: mabn <github@mabn.pl>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:41:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 153/156] [barreplay] H125: no smoke trails behind missiles,
 starbursts and debris (toggle3 0x200000)

speed62's late window: making and updating the trails (unsynced projectiles,
CSmokeTrailProjectile) is ~0.2% of the main thread, and freeing projectiles
another 0.28% of which they are a part. The one thing a synced projectile
takes from its trail is the trail's useAirLos, which the trail's constructor
computes from its midpoint ((pos1 + pos2) * 0.5f, more than 10 elmos above
CGround::GetApproximateHeight); BrH125::AirLos computes it without the trail.
In a trail's place the projectile holds a tag never dereferenced, so each
'is there a trail' test answers as before and the old smoke position and
direction advance exactly as they did.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
